frankensim-shell-assembly-options-v1
# A VIOLA body for the material_strings shell route, table shell-assembly-h6.5.tsv (25 parts, 11796 nodes, 19002 triangles,
# 48 ties): published values (LOC Cassavetti back length and bouts, the caliper f-hole drawing of the same viola, Johannsson's
# viola table, Medium column) mapped onto the il Cannone specimen tables; every mapped value and every ASSUMPTION is in the
# specimen's PROVENANCE.tsv. Not a scanned viola.
# Every choice is cannone-h6.assembly's except the projection work and the one bridge: the window is the same 15 Hz-5 kHz
# (the spruce pack's source band ends at 5 kHz), the same two violin shell packs.
window-hz 15 5000
# The v4 maximum, 2^41 terms; the documented count for 11796 nodes, 19002 triangles, 256 modes and one bridge is about 1.7e12.
projection-work 2199023255552
reference-thickness-m 0.003
pack spruce @body
pack maple violin-maple-sycamore-sonderegger2013-shell.fsmatpk
# One string per card (a 1-string card needs a 1-bridge profile). The string meets the bridge at this point (x, y) [m] of the
# table (string-contacts.tsv of the specimen: spacing 36 mm C to A, Johannsson); it drives its bridge node along x.
bridge-component bridge
bridge-direction 1 0 0
# C string
bridge -0.018000 -0.049250
